{"excerpt_id":"ex_ff9fbb4f8527_017","source_id":"src_ff9fbb4f8527","source_hash":"8125bad030ffebd4e20366121c83e0487c06c33b2fe5eb554bd3e84f45b6aafa","text":"{\n\"TransactionType\" : \"NFTokenModify\" ,\n\"Account\" : \"rHb9CJAWyB4rj91VRWn96DkukG4bwdtyTh\" ,\n\"Owner\" : \"rogue5HnPRSszD9CWGSUz8UGHMVwSSKF6\" ,\n\"Fee\" : \"10\" ,\n\"Sequence\" : 33 ,\n\"NFTokenID\" : \"0008C350C182B4F213B82CCFA4C6F59AD76F0AFCFBDF04D5A048C0A300000007\" ,\n\"URI\" : \"697066733A2F2F62616679626569636D6E73347A736F6C686C6976346C746D6E356B697062776373637134616C70736D6C6179696970666B73746B736D3472746B652F5665742E706E67\"\n}","location_hint":"paragraph 230","char_start":4919,"char_end":5334,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:34:00.991Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_ff9fbb4f8527_018","source_id":"src_ff9fbb4f8527","source_hash":"8125bad030ffebd4e20366121c83e0487c06c33b2fe5eb554bd3e84f45b6aafa","text":"In addition to the common fields , NFTokenModify transactions use the following fields:","location_hint":"paragraph 232","char_start":5358,"char_end":5445,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:34:00.991Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_ff9fbb4f8527_019","source_id":"src_ff9fbb4f8527","source_hash":"8125bad030ffebd4e20366121c83e0487c06c33b2fe5eb554bd3e84f45b6aafa","text":"Field JSON Type Internal Type Required? Description","location_hint":"paragraph 233","char_start":5449,"char_end":5500,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:34:00.991Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_ff9fbb4f8527_020","source_id":"src_ff9fbb4f8527","source_hash":"8125bad030ffebd4e20366121c83e0487c06c33b2fe5eb554bd3e84f45b6aafa","text":"Owner String - Address AccountID No Address of the owner of the NFT. If the Account and Owner are the same address, omit this field.","location_hint":"paragraph 234","char_start":5504,"char_end":5636,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:34:00.991Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_ff9fbb4f8527_021","source_id":"src_ff9fbb4f8527","source_hash":"8125bad030ffebd4e20366121c83e0487c06c33b2fe5eb554bd3e84f45b6aafa","text":"NFTokenID String - Hexadecimal UInt256 Yes The unique identfier of the NFT to modify.","location_hint":"paragraph 235","char_start":5638,"char_end":5723,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:34:00.991Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_ff9fbb4f8527_022","source_id":"src_ff9fbb4f8527","source_hash":"8125bad030ffebd4e20366121c83e0487c06c33b2fe5eb554bd3e84f45b6aafa","text":"URI String - Hexadecimal Blob No Up to 256 bytes of arbitrary data. In JSON, this should be encoded as a string of hexadecimal. You can use the xrpl.convertStringToHex utility to convert a URI to its hexadecimal equivalent. This is intended to be a URI that points to the data or metadata associated with the NFT. The contents could decode to an HTTP or HTTPS URL, an IPFS URI, a magnet link, immediate data encoded as an RFC 2379 \"data\" URL , or even an issuer-specific encoding. The URI is not checked for validity. If you do not specify a URI, the existing URI is deleted.","location_hint":"paragraph 236","char_start":5725,"char_end":6300,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:34:00.991Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_ff9fbb4f8527_023","source_id":"src_ff9fbb4f8527","source_hash":"8125bad030ffebd4e20366121c83e0487c06c33b2fe5eb554bd3e84f45b6aafa","text":"Besides errors that can occur for all transactions, NFTokenModify transactions can result in the following transaction result codes :","location_hint":"paragraph 238","char_start":6317,"char_end":6450,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:34:00.991Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_ff9fbb4f8527_024","source_id":"src_ff9fbb4f8527","source_hash":"8125bad030ffebd4e20366121c83e0487c06c33b2fe5eb554bd3e84f45b6aafa","text":"tecNO_PERMISSION The tfMutable flag wasn&#x27;t enabled, so you can&#x27;t update the URI field. You can also receive this error if the Account field isn&#x27;t an issuer or authorized minter of the NFT.","location_hint":"paragraph 240","char_start":6480,"char_end":6683,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:34:00.991Z"}
